
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  blue-data-web-source — Content Addressing & Dedup
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  PART 1 — Deterministic chunk_id from URL
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  URL      : https://tech.example.com/batteries
  sha256   : f43a68a0488ca21f95f2bc2f12b82987d74687987d61eb0d4390f4cedcb1d101
  page_id  : web_f43a68a0488ca21f  (first 16 hex chars)
  chunk_00 : web_f43a68a0488ca21f_chunk_0000
  chunk_01 : web_f43a68a0488ca21f_chunk_0001

  ✓  Ingest produced 3 chunks
  ✓    web_f43a68a0488ca21f_chunk_0000
  ✓    web_f43a68a0488ca21f_chunk_0001
  ✓    web_f43a68a0488ca21f_chunk_0002

  PART 2 — Re-ingest same URL (safe idempotency)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ✓  First ingest : ['web_f43a68a0488ca21f_chunk_0000', 'web_f43a68a0488ca21f_chunk_0001', 'web_f43a68a0488ca21f_chunk_0002']
  ✓  Second ingest: ['web_f43a68a0488ca21f_chunk_0000', 'web_f43a68a0488ca21f_chunk_0001', 'web_f43a68a0488ca21f_chunk_0002']
  ✓  chunk_id values are identical — upsert overwrites, no duplicates

  PART 3 — Redirect: UTM-tracked URL → canonical URL
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Source URL (fetched) : https://tech.example.com/batteries?utm_source=newsletter
  Final URL (canonical): https://tech.example.com/batteries

  ✓  Records produced: 3
  ✓  page_id  (actual)  : web_f43a68a0488ca21f
  ✓  page_id  (expected): web_f43a68a0488ca21f  ← sha256(final_url)
  ✓  page_id derived from final_url, not original URL
  ✓  Fetching with UTM params produces the same chunk IDs as the canonical URL

  PART 4 — Different domain URL → different chunk IDs
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  URL A chunk_id : web_f43a68a0488ca21f_chunk_0000
  URL B chunk_id : web_6e8e1d19ef932d16_chunk_0000
  ✓  Same content, different URL → different chunk IDs (URL is the identity key)
  ✓  Note: with a FreshnessStore, cross-URL content dedup will skip the 2nd ingest at pipeline level

  ID SCHEME COMPARISON: web-source vs doc-source
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Property                       web-source             doc-source
  ────────────────────────────── ────────────────────── ────────────────────
  Hash input                     sha256(final_url)      sha256(file bytes)
  ID format                      web_{h16}_chunk_NNNN   doc_{h16}_chunk_NNNNNN
  Chunk # padding                4 digits (0000)        6 digits (000000)
  Re-ingest same                 same IDs (upsert)      same IDs (upsert)
  UTM redirect                   → canonical final_url  N/A

